---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import NetworkMotif from '../components/NetworkMotif.astro';
---

<Base
  title="About · Alex Trubey"
  description="Alex Trubey is a PhD student in economics at the University of Toronto, working on networks and information."
  active="about"
>
  <div class="frame">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="kicker">The author</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="cols">
      <div class="bio prose">
        <p>
          I am a PhD student in economics at the University of Toronto, working on networks and
          information: how the pattern of who connects to who shapes what markets know, what they
          reward, and who gets ahead.
        </p>
        <p>
          Before Toronto I completed an MA at Columbia, where I wrote a theory of endogenous
          network formation in information markets under Evan Sadler, and a BA at Chung-Ang
          University in Seoul, where I mapped the collaboration networks of YouTube creators.
        </p>
        <p>
          Hockey, and sports analytics in general, is my other interest.
          <a href="https://alex-trubey.github.io/fabric-of-the-nhl/">The Fabric of the NHL</a>, an
          interactive map of every teammate relationship in the modern league, is the first public
          piece of that work.
        </p>
        <p>
          I also write (as often as I can) about everything and anything else on my Substack,
          <a href="https://alextrubey.substack.com">No Fixed Position</a>.
        </p>
        <p class="actions">
          <a class="btn" href="/cv/alex-trubey-cv.pdf">Curriculum Vitae (PDF)</a>
          <a class="btn" href="mailto:ajtrubey@gmail.com">ajtrubey@gmail.com</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <NetworkMotif class="about-motif" />
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .cols {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1.6fr 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    align-items: start;
    padding-block: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
  }

  .actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.7rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
  }

  .cols :global(.about-motif) {
    max-width: 300px;
    width: 100%;
    justify-self: end;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .cols {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .cols :global(.about-motif) {
      max-width: 230px;
      justify-self: start;
    }
  }
</style>
